.TH MKBDROM 8 "udftools" "System Management Commands"

.SH NAME
mkbdrom \(em create UDF 2.50 BD-ROM images from a source directory

.SH SYNOPSIS
.BI "mkbdrom --source " directory " [--label " label "] [--disc-capacity " blocks "] [--blocksize " bytes "] " output.iso

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mkbdrom
creates a UDF 2.50 image with a Metadata Partition suitable for BD-ROM style
layouts directly from a source directory. The source tree is packed into the
image without mounting an intermediate filesystem.

The tool is intended for authoring Blu-ray compatible images on macOS,
including PS4 and PS5 workflows that require UDF 2.50 metadata partition
layout. The source directory typically contains a
.I BDMV
directory and an optional
.I CERTIFICATE
directory.

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--source " directory
Path to the source directory whose contents will be packed into the output
image. Hidden files and directories are skipped.

.TP
.BI "--label " label
Set both the logical volume identifier and volume identifier for the image.
If omitted, the default label is
.IR BLURAY .

.TP
.BI "--disc-capacity " blocks
Set the target image size in logical blocks. The value must be large enough to
hold both the packed file data and the UDF metadata structures. If omitted,
.B mkbdrom
automatically chooses the minimum required size.

.TP
.BI "--blocksize " bytes
Set the logical block size in bytes. The default is
.IR 2048 .

.TP
.B -h, --help
Display usage information.

.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Create a minimum-size BD-ROM image from a prepared content tree:
.RS
.B mkbdrom --source /path/to/content output.iso
.RE

.TP
Create a 25 GB single-layer BD-R sized image with an explicit label:
.RS
.B mkbdrom --source /path/to/content --label BLURAY --disc-capacity 12219392 output.iso
.RE

.SH NOTES
The generated image uses UDF revision 2.50 with a Type 2 Metadata Partition
Map. This is the layout expected by read-only BD-ROM style consumers.

Common Blu-ray capacities in 2048-byte blocks:
.RS
.TP
12219392
25 GB BD-R single layer
.TP
24438784
50 GB BD-R dual layer
.RE

.SH FILES
.TP
.I BDMV/
Blu-ray disc content tree.
.TP
.I CERTIFICATE/
Optional Blu-ray certificate tree.

.SH SEE ALSO
.BR mkudffs (8),
.BR udfinfo (1),
.BR udflabel (8)